extends RefCounted

# Real rocks, minerals and ices found (or measured from orbit) on each world, for the Sample Lab minigame
# (scripts/sample_lab.gd). Every reading comes from the real material's properties, and every sample names the
# mission that found it, so the instruments always "agree" with each other the way they would in a real lab.
#
# Readings, by instrument (each one only shows if your probe carries that instrument):
#   camera        color and texture, like a rover's mast camera (Mastcam, Navcam)
#   arm           a close-up through a hand lens, like Curiosity's MAHLI on the end of its arm
#   spectrometer  the infrared spectrum: dips ("absorption bands") at wavelengths that fingerprint minerals.
#                 "bands" lists [wavelength in micrometers, depth 0 to 1, width in micrometers]
#   thermal       how fast it warms and cools (thermal inertia), like Mars Odyssey's THEMIS
#   mass_spec     what it's made of, like Curiosity's SAM and Cassini's INMS
#   drill         what drilling into it feels like (hardness), like Curiosity's drill
#
# Band positions are the standard laboratory values (USGS and RELAB spectral libraries): pyroxene near 1 and
# 2 µm, olivine one broad band near 1.05 µm, water ice at 1.5 and 2.0 µm, hydrated minerals near 1.4 and 1.9 µm,
# clays add 2.3 µm, carbonates near 2.3 to 2.5 µm, methane ice at 1.7, 2.2, 2.3 and 3.3 µm. The wavelengths
# are real; the depths are rounded for drawing.

